{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005205-a-disney-parody","id":1005205,"title":"A Disney Parody","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-18T19:54:44-08:00","id":1005205,"title":"A Disney Parody","content":"I have an idea an idea for a antagonist that is either a independent corporation or a subsidiary of PENTEX. It is basically a parody of The Walt Disney Corporation that serves the Wyrm. My basic idea is that they spread Wyrm taint through subliminal messages they hide throughout their movies, whose audience are mostly children and their families. I have posted their history. Feel free to give me your criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-21-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T00:00:06-08:00","id":1006031,"title":"","content":"<br /> If you were to ask any person on the street if they knew what Gronski Entertainment is you would get an immediate yes. Gronski Entertainment is a film company that is well known for both its live-action movies and especially it\u2019s animated ones. Among their famous characters is Captain Salt the Pirate, The Three Knights, and Sheriff Buckshot Jones and his dog sidekick Buckeye. Ironically, Buckeye became the official mascot of the company. But, if you were to ask a Garou he would give you a completely different answer. He would say that Gronski Entertainment is evil, a puppet of the Wyrm. This is true. Gronski Entertainment spreads Wyrm Taint through subliminal messages it hides throughout it\u2019s movies. Gronski Entertainment is currently headed by Donald Bowers, who seeks to cause the Apocalypse to end, what he feels to be, a horrid and wicked world. He also believes that the Wyrm is a great tool to meet this end and serves him willingly along with the rest of Gronski\u2019s Board of Directors. To understand how this company fell from grace, you need to learn it\u2019s history. It is a tale of a man\u2019s great legacy being twisted and corrupted by his offspring and how a seemingly innocent company could actually be extremely evil.<br /> <br /> Gronski Entertainment was founded by Marceli Gronski, a Polish immigrant who arrived in the country in the year 1919. Before founding his company, Marceli drew cartoons for New York newspaper called The Courier. Marceli drew many cartoons, but his favorite was Captain Salt, a bumbling pirate. In 1926, Marceli went to a movie theater to watch a movie not knowing what he was about to see would change his whole destiny. Before the movie started, a cartoon short played. Marceli was amazed; right on the screen was a moving cartoon. After the movie, Marceli realized that he could try to bring his creations to the big screen. He immediately started looking for work at one of the animation companies that were around at the time. But every single one of them rejected his application. Marceli, not being discouraged, decided to do the cartoons in his apartment and get his friend, Jules Winter, an Irish immigrant to help. In 1928, they managed to get their first short, The Treasure Hunt, to a few theaters in the state. This short, which stared Captain Salt, was a success and the theaters that Marceli and Jules sold it to wanted more shorts. The two then made three more shorts, all of which stared Captain Salt, and sold them to the theaters. The money they made from these shorts helped spare them from the worst part of the Great Depression and helped them by an office in a small town outside of New York City called Maple Wood in 1931.<br /> <br /> For the next fifteen years Marceli and Jules worked on shorts and created characters that still are major parts of the company like Three Knights, who are chivalrous but cowardly knights, and Sheriff Buckshot and his dog Buckeye. They also had more and more employees, mostly fellow cartoonists, join up with them. In 1946, he met in feel in love with a woman named Patty O\u2019Hara and married her two years later. This marriage ended prematurely when Patty died giving birth in 1954. Marceli was then surprised to find out that his wife gave birth to triplets before dying. He named these triplets Bud, Robby and Duncan. <br /> When Marceli was 51, his company had over 5,000 employees and had their cartoon shorts playing in theaters across the country. Marceli then decided to do something he never did before, make a movie. After five years of development Sheriff Buckshot the Movie came out to a great reception. This led to a whole series of movies, both animated and live-action being made by the company, whose name was changed from Gronski Animation Studio to Gronski Entertainment. Unfortunatley, tragedy struck the company when Marceli passed away at the age of 71, leaving his three sons in charge. The first thing the triplets did was move the company\u2019s headquarters back to NYC and immediately lay off 100 workers. What no one knew is that during the boy\u2019s college years they ended up a fraternity that served the Wyrm and thus, got tainted by it. The boys immediately started to spread the taint across the company by firing the old Board of Directors and replacing most of them with friends they knew from college, mostly fellow servants of the Wyrm. They also decided to start tainting their customers by hiding subliminal messages throughout their movies, a practice that remains to this day. Under the triplet\u2019s the company did surprisingly well and eventually grew to have over 50,000 employees. Many changes to the company besides the relocation and New Board happened during this time. Among these was making Buckeye, Sheriff Buckshot\u2019s sidekick, into the company mascot after they noticed that Buckshot, who was basically an intelligent, but mute, dog was more popular than the companies\u2019 current mascot at the time, Captain Salt. The company continued to taint people under the noses of the Garou, who didn\u2019t think a company like them could possibly be Wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> By 2000, all three of the triplets were dead, all of them killed by their own vices. The ensuing power struggle was quenched when Donald Bowers, one of the few board members who were not from the triplet\u2019s inner circle, took over. Bowers, who was also a Wyrm servant, continued placing subliminal messaging through the movies they produced while trying to avoid the attention of the Garou. In 2008, the Recession hit and nearly drove Gronski out of business. PENTEX, seeing the opportunity of acquiring another subsidiary, tried to buy out the company. Donald however, rejected their deal and desperately searched for a way to keep his business from going bankrupt. In 2009, Gronski released a new movie that managed to save the company from bankruptcy. This movie however, broke the biggest rule of the company. Don\u2019t place more than one subliminal message in the movie. As a result, the Garou found out about the corporation\u2019s true nature. Donald, realizing that a Garou attack was inevitable, had the companies\u2019 headquarters moved to Miami, Florida, where it is located to this day. Even though the company changed locations, it did not take Monkeywrenchers very long to find out where they moved to. What followed was a series of hackings, sabotage, and practical jokes that hindered 3 of the company\u2019s projects. In 2013, half the Board of Directors died in a plane crash on their way to Los Angles. What followed was an eight month squabble among the surviving Board Members over who to appoint to the Board. Pentex, seeing an opportunity to sabotage Gronski, sent in a mole named Pete Fisher, who was immediately placed on the Board.<br /> <br /> Gronski Entertainment is currently working on three new projects while continuing to weather the attacks thrown at them by the Monkeywrenchers, whose sabotage attempts are becoming more and more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}